hnat: dispatch short packets to a high-priority queue

When short_pkt_toggle is enabled, TCP ACKs (payload 0) and small UDP
packets (payload <= short_pkt_len) are dispatched to the high-priority
hardware queue short_pkt_qid on any path (no PPPQ requirement), so
games and other latency-sensitive small flows get prioritized even on
2.5G direct ports.

Flows that already carry an explicit queue id via skb->mark (custom
priority rules / device rules) keep their queue; auto detection only
applies to otherwise unclassified traffic. Only genuine short packets
are redirected, so the bulk packets of a classified flow still use the
queue their rule selected.

The "unclassified" test no longer uses MTK_QDMA_QUEUE_MASK. That macro
is not a queue-bit mask: it was GENMASK(15, 0) while the 64-queue
rework (999-zzz-5113, since dropped in favour of the official
per-SoC queue count in 999-eth-56) was in the tree, and is now
(eth->soc->num_tx_queues - 1). Either way it does not describe the
queue bits HNAT uses, and the per-SoC form cannot even be evaluated
here (`eth` in this scope is a struct ethhdr). HNAT_QDMA_QUEUE_MASK is
used instead, restricted to the bits below HNAT_EXCEPTION_BIT (bit
0..6 on netsys v2/v3, bit 0..3 on v1.x), matching how the HQoS path
reads the id back, and compared against MAX_PPPQ_QUEUE_NUM, the
threshold the PPPQ/HQoS code above uses to tell an explicit queue hint
from a per-port queue.

The check is deliberately not gated on !IS_HQOS_MODE. HQoS is what
turns the skb->mark -> QDMA queue mapping on in the first place, and
luci-app-eqos-mtk sets qos_toggle to 1 (HQoS) right before enabling
short_pkt_toggle, so excluding it made the feature a no-op for every
user configuring it from the UI.

Signed-off-by: hxlls <hxlls@users.noreply.github.com>
---

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat_nf_hook.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat_nf_hook.c
index a1675f4..2a4d766 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat_nf_hook.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat_nf_hook.c
@@ -3074,7 +3074,72 @@ hnat_entry_bind:
 	else
 		qid = 0;
 
-	if (IS_PPPQ_MODE && IS_PPPQ_PATH(dev, skb) && port_id >= 0) {
+	/* Short-packet QoS: TCP ACKs and small UDP packets are dispatched to a
+	 * high-priority queue on any path (no PPPQ requirement), so games and
+	 * other latency-sensitive small flows get prioritized even on 2.5G
+	 * direct ports.
+	 */
+	/* Flows that already carry an explicit queue id via skb->mark (custom
+	 * priority rules / device rules) keep that queue; auto detection only
+	 * applies to otherwise unclassified traffic, i.e. to flows whose
+	 * mark is below MAX_PPPQ_QUEUE_NUM, exactly how the PPPQ/HQoS code
+	 * above classifies them.  Note that only genuine short packets are
+	 * redirected below - bulk packets of a classified flow keep the queue
+	 * their rule selected.
+	 *
+	 * Deliberately not gated on !IS_HQOS_MODE: HQoS mode is exactly what
+	 * turns the skb->mark -> QDMA queue mapping on, so luci-app-eqos-mtk
+	 * sets qos_toggle to 1 (HQoS) before enabling short_pkt_toggle.
+	 * Excluding HQoS here would make the feature a no-op for every user
+	 * who configures it from the UI.
+	 *
+	 * HNAT_QDMA_QUEUE_MASK covers only the queue bits, i.e. everything
+	 * below HNAT_EXCEPTION_BIT (netsys v2/v3 use bit 0..6, v1.x bit 0..3),
+	 * which is how the HQoS path reads the id back. Using MTK_QDMA_QUEUE_MASK
+	 * here instead is not an option: it is redefined per kernel series (was
+	 * GENMASK(15, 0), now (eth->soc->num_tx_queues - 1)) and the per-SoC
+	 * form cannot even be evaluated here (`eth` is a struct ethhdr).
+	 */
+	if (short_pkt_toggle &&
+	    (skb->mark & HNAT_QDMA_QUEUE_MASK) < MAX_PPPQ_QUEUE_NUM) {
+		if (h_proto == ETH_P_IP) {
+			iph = (struct iphdr *)(skb_network_header(skb) + h_offset);
+			if (iph->protocol == IPPROTO_TCP) {
+				tcph = (struct tcphdr *)((u8 *)iph + iph->ihl * 4);
+				payload_len = be16_to_cpu(iph->tot_len) -
+					      iph->ihl * 4 - __tcp_hdrlen(tcph);
+				if (payload_len == 0) {
+					qid = short_pkt_qid;
+					pr_info_once("hnat shortpkt: TCP ACK -> qid %d\n", qid);
+				}
+			} else if (iph->protocol == IPPROTO_UDP) {
+				payload_len = be16_to_cpu(iph->tot_len) -
+					      iph->ihl * 4 - sizeof(struct udphdr);
+				if (payload_len <= short_pkt_len) {
+					qid = short_pkt_qid;
+					pr_info_once("hnat shortpkt: UDP len=%u -> qid %d\n",
+						payload_len, qid);
+				}
+			}
+		} else if (h_proto == ETH_P_IPV6) {
+			ip6h = (struct ipv6hdr *)(skb_network_header(skb) + h_offset);
+			if (ip6h->nexthdr == NEXTHDR_TCP) {
+				tcph = (struct tcphdr *)((u8 *)ip6h + sizeof(struct ipv6hdr));
+				payload_len = be16_to_cpu(ip6h->payload_len) - __tcp_hdrlen(tcph);
+				if (payload_len == 0) {
+					qid = short_pkt_qid;
+					pr_info_once("hnat shortpkt: IPv6 TCP ACK -> qid %d\n", qid);
+				}
+			} else if (ip6h->nexthdr == NEXTHDR_UDP) {
+				payload_len = be16_to_cpu(ip6h->payload_len) - sizeof(struct udphdr);
+				if (payload_len <= short_pkt_len) {
+					qid = short_pkt_qid;
+					pr_info_once("hnat shortpkt: IPv6 UDP len=%u -> qid %d\n",
+						payload_len, qid);
+				}
+			}
+		}
+	} else if (IS_PPPQ_MODE && IS_PPPQ_PATH(dev, skb) && port_id >= 0) {
 		if (h_proto == ETH_P_IP) {
 			iph = (struct iphdr *)(skb_network_header(skb) + h_offset);
 			if (iph->protocol == IPPROTO_TCP) {
